{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788472972213918001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"salmon-abominable-pupa","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4b06e92bf4d43203ee9af8a8e8fae276468dd2045335944bdd45a3bda0fd4001","event_uuid":"e8287738-5c4a-4d08-a7fe-b20b4bf47631","position":{"commit_sha":"6bd3c8eb3da2dd883b8c0d60aedef7cecd2f5968","position":"1788469523116095726-e8287738-5c4a-4d08-a7fe-b20b4bf47631"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7ccd2479bdce6069109e4c44c7d9c868f4f5e14a4193e9e1f8f3bf3a41cdae53","event_uuid":"8615cf0d-6693-4248-b195-0d4e583fe999","position":{"commit_sha":"cd813d15ccd6ac77f48b64f920fe76b7b3af78dd","position":"1788469563839691394-8615cf0d-6693-4248-b195-0d4e583fe999"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1fa9b1d305ac865a1668738ce5f80a9b8f0332de26c8b19716453ce3c8c1f9bd","event_uuid":"fdd59bbd-441f-420d-94c9-7275679728db","position":{"commit_sha":"73e772a9743b3b85788f31c82f18f31058da2a52","position":"1788469611993200336-fdd59bbd-441f-420d-94c9-7275679728db"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a7a5c4a4247c33715723fedb453cc3ead2c61d4dc4108d1470a665ab2bb5a923","event_uuid":"aca6940c-9cc2-462a-a6f3-4a6926a1485b","position":{"commit_sha":"24bc60a819d769c92d30ee5d511dfbc0241ab8c9","position":"1788469625354062658-aca6940c-9cc2-462a-a6f3-4a6926a1485b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788469523116095726,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8615cf0d-6693-4248-b195-0d4e583fe999","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"08ab-60d2-3082-4b47"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCode review already routes changed Terraform to the `code-review-iac` overlay, but its Pass-1 overlay and Pass-2 verifier have only generic repository tools. This slice reuses the tool-session contract created by `forcible-diminished-lamb` [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb] so IaC findings can cite and independently re-check whole-module evidence. It changes no behavior for other diffs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Thread `assemble_diff.outputs.changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`; its constructor already stores this field, but the production gate dispatcher currently omits it.\n- In both Round A and Round B, create a fresh Terraform tool session only for an included `code-review-iac` criterion when the changed set contains `.tf`, `.tf.json`, or an explicitly changed `.tfvars`. Supply the `lookup_declaration` and `resolve_reference` tools from the prerequisite. The base reviewer and every other overlay receive no Terraform tools.\n- Scope the session from changed paths, then use the prerequisite's whole affected-module/local-closure rules. A changed `.tfvars` remains direct evidence only and is never treated as an automatically selected input.\n- After Pass-1 merge, expose a new session to `code-review-verify` only when a merged finding is attributed to `code-review-iac` and the changed set has Terraform scope. The verifier receives the Pass-1 receipt as evidence but must issue its own query; there is no inherited answer or query ledger.\n- The coach and deterministic decision steps receive no Terraform tools.\n- Merge concrete/module-membership reads into the call's `_usage.distinct_fetches`. Include the concrete Terraform files read in the code-review sidecar's reviewed-file `deps` so region-gated re-review memory cannot reuse evidence after a module dependency changes.\n- Keep missing-extra behavior fail-open: code review continues through its existing generic path, with no advertised Terraform tools. An advertised tool failure returns the prerequisite's closed abstention and cannot itself create or block a finding.\n- Do not add a scanner stage or originate findings from the index. The IaC overlay remains the finder; grounding only answers its explicit queries.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nThe slice is independently releasable after its prerequisite: a Terraform diff receives query-grounded IaC review end to end, while all non-IaC requests remain byte-compatible. It reuses the existing overlay routing and generic per-call tool-provider seam instead of creating a Terraform-specific review engine.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nNo new parser, source-network logic, corroborator executable, prompt change, standalone validation, Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution, or non-IaC tool exposure.\n\n## Failure-disposition contract\n\n- Missing `grounding-terraform` extra: non-fatal capability absence; advertise no tools and complete the ordinary review.\n- Unsupported/ambiguous/dynamic Terraform question: return ABSTAIN; the LLM may verify directly from files but the tool supplies no positive claim.\n- Parser/path/limit/timeout failure: return ABSTAIN and preserve the existing review result; do not reinterpret it as a clean module or nonexistent symbol.\n- Internal routing/session construction defect: surface through existing gate error handling rather than silently attaching tools to a broader step.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Production dispatch passes the exact assembled `changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`, and a Round-A changed-`.tf` integration test observes both Terraform tools only on `code-review-iac`.\n- [ ] A Round-B escalation test observes the same tool surface and whole-module resolution when IaC is recommended rather than glob-selected, without running the overlay twice.\n- [ ] A merged IaC finding makes `code-review-verify` receive a distinct Terraform query session; a verifier tool call returns a fresh receipt rather than reusing the Pass-1 result.\n- [ ] Base review, non-IaC overlays, coach, a Python-only diff, and an IaC review with no IaC findings advertise no Terraform tools.\n- [ ] A changed `.tfvars` can be queried as direct structural evidence, and a test proves its value is not injected into module variables or used to resolve a computed reference.\n- [ ] Code-review usage and sidecar dependency tests contain the concrete sibling/local-module files read; modifying one invalidates the recorded dependency hash while an unrelated non-Terraform file does not.\n- [ ] Missing-extra and every prerequisite ABSTAIN outcome leave the ordinary code-review decision path intact and never become a synthetic IaC finding.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, this ticket, and the prerequisite's tool/receipt contract [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb].\n- Preconditions: a real assembled diff with one changed root `.tf`, an unchanged sibling declaration, a local child module, and captured Round-A/Round-B/verifier requests.\n- Production path: production gate dispatch → real `CodeReviewBatchRunner` → real tool session; only the model result is faked.\n- Tier: workflow integration, because the contract crosses trigger selection, overlay batch dispatch, merge, verifier routing, usage, and sidecar dependency capture.\n- Oracle: exact tool-name sets per request, distinct receipt/query-session ids across passes, resolved sibling evidence, and changed dependency digest after editing a read file.\n- Negative controls: an equivalent `.py` diff and a Terraform diff with no IaC finding leave base/other overlays/verifier/coach tool-free.\n- CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"pass changed files and scoped tool provider into production code review"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py","reason":"inject/finalize Terraform sessions only for the IaC overlay"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"identify merged IaC findings for verifier routing"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"include grounding reads in reviewed-file dependency hashes"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"Round-A/Round-B/Pass-2 routing and dependency integration"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"production code-review workflow regression coverage"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document code-review routing and failure behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","08ab-60d2-3082-4b47"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["terraform","grounding","llm","optional","code-review"],"ticket_id":"afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02","ticket_type":"story","title":"Ground code-review IaC findings in changed Terraform modules","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k routing","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Round-A, Round-B, verifier, and negative routing"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k tfvars","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"tfvars remains direct evidence only"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k deps","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"usage and sidecar dependency invalidation"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k \"missing_extra or abstain\"","dd_id":"AC7","dd_text":"missing-extra and abstention preserve ordinary decision path"}]},"source_event_uuids":["e8287738-5c4a-4d08-a7fe-b20b4bf47631","8615cf0d-6693-4248-b195-0d4e583fe999","fdd59bbd-441f-420d-94c9-7275679728db","aca6940c-9cc2-462a-a6f3-4a6926a1485b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788472972213918001,"uuid":"ac60655b-c79f-41d1-b582-fd92de1ea3d3"}